  "term": "EFA",
  "definition": "EFA stands for exploratory factor analysis, a statistical method used in early scale development to examine how questionnaire items cluster together and to help decide which items should be retained. In this study, it was used before confirmatory factor analysis to check the structure of the scale items.",
